    <title>Flood alert: River Wye in Herefordshire</title>
    <link href="https://cheltenham-od.uk/cheltenham-flood-warnings/history#http://environment.data.gov.uk/flood-monitoring/id/floods/031WAF119"/>
    <id>https://cheltenham-od.uk/cheltenham-flood-warnings/history#http://environment.data.gov.uk/flood-monitoring/id/floods/031WAF119</id>
    <author>
      <name>Environment Agency</name>
    </author>
    <summary>Forecast high river levels overnight may lead to flooding.
Flooding is possible from overnight on Saturday 24 October into Sunday 25 October.
Flooding may affect low lying land and roads along the River Wye from Hay on Wye to Ross on Wye. Other locations affected may include the A438 between Letton &amp; Willersey, Byford, Bredwardine &amp; Hereford. Road closures &amp; diversions on the A438 may be in force. Predicted peaks:- Hay on Wye 1.8m to 2.1m on 25/10 AM, Bredwardine 3.7m to 4.0m on 25/10 AM, Belmont 3.8 to 4.1m on 25/10 AM, Old Wye Bridge 3.3m to 3.6m on 25/10 AM, Mordiford 3.4m to 3.7m on 25/10 PM, and Ross on Wye 2.9m to 3.2m on 25/10 PM.
We are closely monitoring the situation .
Take care and avoid walking, cycling or driving through flood water.  
This message will be updated by 10:00AM on Sunday 25 October or as the situation changes.
 · County: Gloucestershire, Herefordshire</summary>
    <updated>2026-10-25T08:45:09Z</updated>
